WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.650
Those blasted Foundation rats had done it
again...

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:11.650
SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile, sat
in its tank of highly concentrated acid and

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.160
seethed at the world it had been placed in.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.720
And what a miserable, terrible world it was.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:24.140
He hated it, and he hated every single soul
that occupied it - and especially the hypocritical

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.970
monsters in lab coats that ran this sham of
an organization.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:34.140
Whenever the reptile wasn’t speaking - normally
to bark threats and profanities at its human

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.070
jailers - it was quietly listening, taking
everything in, and how the things it heard

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:45.740
made its blood boil more than the corrosive
fluid forever eating into its carapace.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:51.450
What high-minded ideas these worthless apes
had about themselves: “We’re cold, not

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.450
cruel.”

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.450
Ha!

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.629
What a sick joke...

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:59.100
Every moment for the reptile was a different
kind of hell.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.449
The baseline of existence was a certain dull,
fizzling pain as he melted as quickly as his

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:06.070
cells could divide.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.899
His only reprieve from this was to be dragged
into a testing chamber for some even worse

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:18.020
pain: Perhaps burned, or sliced, or chewed
at by a mutant rabbit, or crushed by bananas,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:23.459
or torn apart by wires and hooks, or beaten
and bashed by some mad swordsman, or having

00:01:23.459 --> 00:01:27.729
his mind invaded and attacked by a rogue soul
in a cursed necklace.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:33.779
If this was only “Cold”, then the reptile
hated to even imagine what the SCP Foundation

00:01:33.779 --> 00:01:34.930
considered “Cruel.”

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:39.049
After all, there were monsters more powerful
than him out there.

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:43.859
The Hanged King or the Devourer Of Worlds
could handily destroy their wretched ball

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:46.509
of rock if they so chose to.

00:01:46.509 --> 00:01:51.789
He wasn’t the most sadistic or evil of the
beasts these maniacs in white coats had faced.

00:01:51.789 --> 00:01:56.060
Those who warred with him met a quick death
at his claws and fangs.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.829
Would that nightmarish Old Man afford his
victims such a luxury?

00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:03.250
Or that unstoppable psychopath in the old
police car?

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:11.660
And yet, it was his file that bore the addendum:
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:12.769
And why?

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:17.629
Seemingly only because he could take it, and
the Foundation always had new toys it wanted

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:20.230
to test on their favorite punching bag.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:23.760
Of course, he attempted to escape, but wouldn’t
you?

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.569
Is freedom not an inalienable right?

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:30.709
The Foundation would cry, “But look at the
terrible crimes he’s committed!

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:32.599
Look at the lives he’s taken!”

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:34.269
as they always do.

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:38.640
Let he who is without sin draw the first acid
bath.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.769
He knew, on some level, if he were to make
a tally, the Foundation’s crimes would far

00:02:42.769 --> 00:02:44.329
outnumber his own.

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:48.780
The only difference was that they’d deluded
themselves into believing all acts of cruelty

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.280
are permissible in service of their “greater
good.”

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:57.700
If they all had but one head, the reptile
would claw it from their shoulders.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.040
A group of incredibly well-armed and well-armored
guards entered the room, training all their

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.040
weapons on him.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.731
He hadn’t summoned the energy to escape
today, and that meant only one thing: They

00:03:08.731 --> 00:03:11.980
were going to take another swing at killing
him again.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.459
Oh, goody.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:18.760
Another attempt that would leave him momentarily
in absolute agony, and allow neither of them

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.290
to gain any ground.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:24.360
He’d grown numb to attempts on his life
by now.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.160
Whatever they had waiting for him in the other
room, he’d be ready for it.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.109
The guards removed him from his acid bath,
and, while he was still trying to regenerate

00:03:32.109 --> 00:03:36.489
his muscles and nerves enough to move, they
dragged him into the testing chamber.

00:03:36.489 --> 00:03:41.860
It was always a mystery, wondering what they’d
be poking or prodding him with today.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.730
But when he was first dragged into the chamber,
it was...

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.730
Empty.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.970
Those were always the worst ones.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.579
When he was left some sitting duck, waiting
for the Foundation, in their infinite malice,

00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:56.760
to choose the form of the would-be destroyer.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.530
What would be behind Door Number One...

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.680
A box.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:06.810
A large, wooden box was pushed into the room,
and the door closed behind it.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.980
How curious.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.299
The Hard to Destroy Reptile began to approach
the box, sniffing at the air.

00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:17.160
It made no sound in there, but something about
that smell.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.160
Something...

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.979
eerily familiar...

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:21.519
It was different this time.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:26.910
With a soft pop, the box fell apart, its walls
falling in different directions like the petals

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.560
of a blooming flower.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.900
And the second the Hard to Destroy Reptile
saw what lurked inside, it felt an unfamiliar

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:37.669
cold barb of terror hook into the soft, warm
flesh of its heart.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:43.780
The thing inside the box had been called SCP-173
by the SCP Foundation, but that wasn’t how

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.220
the reptile knew it.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.020
It was a primordial nightmare.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.860
An ancient horror.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.139
The stone devil.

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:53.060
The killer in the dark.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:58.240
The Koitern, which had mercilessly and gleefully
slaughtered so much of the reptile’s very

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.629
species, back when 682 was known as the Atanti-ql-Paneu.

00:05:01.629 --> 00:05:04.520
And here it was...

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.860
Ready to finish the job.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:12.310
SCP-682 let out an involuntary screech of
pure horror and fled backwards, keeping its

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.710
eyes fixed on the monster at all times.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:18.770
He moved back until he hit the far wall of
the containment chamber.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.639
Until he could go no further.

00:05:20.639 --> 00:05:23.310
His mind was flooded and his heart was racing.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.960
He never thought he’d see this monster again.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.890
He’d hoped it would never cross his path
again.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:33.780
Perhaps he’d even held out hope that the
abomination had been slain, destroyed, scattered

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:34.780
to the winds.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.840
And yet, here it was, looking at him.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.509
The reptile called out, “You fools.

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:44.330
You have no idea what you’ve done.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.330
This...

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:49.780
Thing, mark my words, it will be your ruin!

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:54.150
It will slaughter every single one of you!”

00:05:54.150 --> 00:06:00.430
But its appeals to reason with its captors,
in their own interest, for once, fell on utterly

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.850
uninterested ears.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:07.150
Six hours of this passed, the reptile spending
every second of it, for the first time in

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.509
a long time, fearing for his life.

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:14.980
A group of observing Foundation scientists
merely noted a peculiar reaction of distress

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:20.819
from 682 and ordered a decorated Mobile Task
Force sharpshooter with a Barrett 50 Caliber

00:06:20.819 --> 00:06:24.600
Sniper Rifle
with armor-piercing rounds to initiate Phase

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.400
2 of the cross test.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:32.460
In a sudden flash of sound and pain, the sharpshooter
blew away both of SCP-682’s staring eyes.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:36.349
The simultaneous instruction went out for
all observing members of personnel to avert

00:06:36.349 --> 00:06:39.130
their gaze, just for a moment.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:44.750
682 could certainly regenerate its eyes quickly,
but nothing was quite as fast as an unobserved

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.040
SCP-173.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:51.880
The reptile screeched in pain as it heard
the monster snapping its body parts, leaving

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.319
it thoroughly mutilated.

00:06:53.319 --> 00:06:59.840
When the group of observing scientists looked
back, they saw it - which is to say, SCP-173

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:06.699
- standing before a heavily damaged SCP-682,
as though incredibly proud of its handiwork.

00:07:06.699 --> 00:07:12.129
Internally, 682 thanked a creator it despised
for the fact that the observers looked back

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:16.610
and spared it from the onslaught that soulless
stone monster had unleashed on it.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:20.729
A scientist working for the Foundation would
later remark, “After review, it appears

00:07:20.729 --> 00:07:27.110
SCP-173 was unable to do lethal damage to
SCP-682 due to a major difference in physical

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.110
size.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:32.830
A possible repeat of this test may be made
if SCP-682 is damaged enough to reduce its

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.710
physical mass to a level equal with SCP-173.”

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.710
But 682 knew, deep down, this wasn’t the
truth.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:45.169
It had nothing to do with physical size: If
the Koitern had truly willed it, he never

00:07:45.169 --> 00:07:46.759
would have left that room.

00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:49.970
The monster only wanted to extend the torment.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:54.110
And this time, SCP-682 wouldn’t let him.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:57.990
He regenerated, adapted, and came back ready.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:04.740
682 developed a number of eyes, far more than
before, that remained fixed on SCP-173, paralyzing

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:05.740
it.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.910
It crawled back up onto the wall and simply
stared.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:12.590
Once again, the observing scientists ordered
the sharpshooter to take aim and open fire.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.620
But this time, the bullets had no effect.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:20.990
SCP-682 has developed a thick, clear carapace
over the surface of its new eyes, ensuring

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:25.889
that nothing would break its eye contact with
that murderous little monster.

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:29.160
This time, it would not lose.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:34.130
But for all the time that 682 stared, 173
said nothing, as always.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:40.030
It just stood there, the strange pattern of
its face, that nasty, bloody Rorschach splotch,

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:42.150
looked almost like a mocking smile.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.040
It conceded nothing.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.960
It seemed to say, “Go on.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.240
Get an eyeful.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:54.370
I have all the time in the universe, and everyone
looks away eventually, even you, Atanti-ql-Paneu.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.740
Let the eternal silence of your brethren be
a lesson to you.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.930
All you will hear is Crunch.”

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:05.910
682 kept up the staring contest for twelve
hours, before it was taken back to its acid

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.320
bath, thoroughly shaken by its experience.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:13.890
It had always despised its terrible captors,
but now, a new shade of darkness had entered

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.560
its narrow emotional lexicon: Fear.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.560
True fear.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.560
An acknowledgment, deep down in its muscle
tissue and guts, that there was something

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.800
out there that could truly hurt it.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:30.270
The terrible Koitern was alive and thirsty
for blood.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:34.950
The researchers who’d conducted this test
considered it an interesting partial success.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:40.150
While 682 was quaking in its tank thinking
about 173, they were brainstorming the best

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:45.540
move to take next, regarding potential pairings
between 682 and 173.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:52.200
A plucky researcher noted that 096 had also
gotten SCP-682 on the ropes, so maybe they

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:57.470
should send in SCP-173 with a photo of SCP-096
taped to its chest.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.980
A member of the O5 Council intervened before
this got too far, saying, “No.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:02.980
Absolutely not.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:08.880
Setting aside the problem of SCP-682, an SCP-173
that cannot be observed for fear of triggering

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:15.150
a response from SCP-096 is a self-perpetuating
catastrophe that the Foundation does not,

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:19.300
under any reasonable circumstances, have the
slightest desire to unleash.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.060
Denied with vehemence.”

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:25.650
The researcher who’d suggested this idea
felt supremely embarrassed, and retired briefly

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:30.170
to one of the employee bathrooms to have a
good cry before returning to the brainstorming

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.340
session.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:36.220
Researcher Maytus, a more experienced member
of personnel, had a stroke of genius.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:40.390
He reminded the assembled researchers that
they’d recently performed another semi-successful

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:45.810
experiment on SCP-682: Using their deadly,
high-precision blades, they were able to slice

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:49.200
and dice 682 into a series of amorphous blobs.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:54.120
Sure, these blobs may have attacked and killed
some D-Classes before reforming into the OG

00:10:54.120 --> 00:11:01.250
Nasty Reptile, but each of these blobs were
the perfect size to be murdered by SCP-173.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:06.080
It eliminated the size differential and put
these two on an even playing field, and on

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:12.250
that even playing field, it stood to reason
that SCP-173 might win.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:17.460
The cross-test was greenlit and a researcher
named Dr. Shenron was put in charge of overseeing

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.940
the operations.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:23.670
And this time, due to Foundation incompetence
and a greater degree of mental preparedness

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:28.600
by SCP-682, they were in for a complete disaster.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:32.650
682 and 173 were brought into the same containment
chamber.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:37.510
682 could feel the latent fear welling up
inside itself, so it did the thing that it

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:41.320
knew the best: It tried to stoke up its rage.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.410
Its hatred.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:46.830
The fury and spite that had kept it going
through so many torturous attempts on its

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:47.830
life.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.910
It would not die at the hands of this stone
monster.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:56.920
And if that was its destiny, then it would
ensure, with its dying wretched breaths, it

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.810
would destroy this terrible beast once and
for all.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:04.190
It would shatter it and ensure it never put
itself back together.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.670
Suddenly, the high-precision blades were deployed.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:11.690
It was an endless volley of cutting that dashed
the two deadly anomalies to pieces like a

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.580
giant As Seen On TV Slap-Chop.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:20.050
Because the machine had been calibrated for
its body, 682 was sliced into 12,000 perfect

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:24.790
cubes, and 173 had been cut into a pile of
lumpy, irregular chunks.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:30.150
A vacuum system was then activated to separate
both anomalies into different chambers, so

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:37.910
173 could reform and begin the assault, but
miraculously for 682, the vacuum system failed.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:43.880
Two D-Classes were sent in to recalibrate
the system, but things quickly got even worse.

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:48.730
Many of the 682 cubes formed the same gelatinous
masses that they did in the previous High

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:53.630
Precision Blades Test, and began attacking
and killing one of the D-Classes.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:57.820
The other, naturally, turned to look at this
horrifying display - Which meant nobody was

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.380
paying attention to SCP-173.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:05.270
Immediately, the Sculpture reformed and snapped
the surviving D-Class’ neck before turning

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:08.040
its attention to SCP-682.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.410
The emergency incineration system failed,
so all the Foundation could hope for was Mutually

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:16.380
Assured Destruction until they got the situation
back under control.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:21.560
However, the Foundation had underestimated
682’s intelligence and tactical reasoning.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:26.600
While the gelatinous, mutated globs of its
flesh attacked 173, smashing and cracking

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:31.680
its concrete body as it killed and splattered
them, the remainder of 682’s flesh formed

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:36.230
a smaller version of itself, which began staring
at 173.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:41.380
This froze the sculpture in place while the
mutated flesh monster smashed into it, slowly

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.960
breaking it down.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:48.240
For the first time in as long as it could
remember, 682 felt genuine glee.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.040
The thrill of revenge.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.770
The glory of an ancient foe vanquished.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:58.200
It would now slay the terrible Koitern, as
its ancestors had tried to do so many times

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.010
before, and failed.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:02.510
But this reptile would not fail.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:07.790
Until, of course, the SCP Foundation - monsters
that they were - decided to put their finger

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.020
on the scale.

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:14.490
The same Foundation Mobile Task Force sharpshooter
who’d been there during the first 173 cross-test

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:18.010
was still there, still ready to carry out
his duties.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:22.190
On the order of the researchers, he fired
another two shots, blowing out the eyes of

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.430
this new, smaller 682.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:30.650
While it regenerated its precious eyes, 173
went on a rampage, mercilessly slaughtering

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.930
every single one of the eyeless blobs of mutated
flesh.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:39.750
It smashed each one beyond repair, until only
it and the smaller 682 remained.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:46.031
Luckily for 682, its eyes regenerated, complete
with the familiar bulletproof covering, just

00:14:46.031 --> 00:14:48.690
in time to hold back 173 from killing it.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:54.360
The two remained locked in a staring contest
of pure hatred for a solid seventeen hours

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.690
before the test was eventually called off.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.080
But the horrors continued!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:04.650
Exhausted by the ordeal already, SCP-682 was
sedated and returned to its containment chamber

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:08.920
without incident, where it regenerated back
to its default state.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.680
Things weren’t so easy with SCP-173.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:16.660
While a team transported it back to its containment
chamber, there was a power outage in the hall,

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.200
and things went dark.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:24.170
And considering SCP-173, in addition to The
Sculpture and The Peanut, could also be nicknamed,

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.540
“Instant Killing Spree, Just Add Darkness!”

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.530
it won’t surprise you to hear there were
no survivors.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:35.040
173 killed everyone in the hall, then escaped
out into the wider facility, causing a site-wide

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:38.630
containment breach and a huge number of casualties.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:43.170
The cause of the electrical short that kickstarted
this massacre was traced back to Dr. Shenron’s

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.340
tampering with the incinerator system.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:50.030
This got the doctor formally reprimanded,
stripped of his titles and his memories, and

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.200
relieved of his duty.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.300
But the worst was still very much to come
for everyone involved.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.600
Including SCP-682.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:04.260
Because the true terrifying potential of SCP-173
was soon going to be unleashed, and when that

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.900
happened, nowhere would be safe.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:11.840
On what was otherwise a very normal day, in
a very normal procedure when a few D-Classes

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:20.040
were sent into SCP-173’s cell, something
extraordinary and terrible happened: SCP-173

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.390
multiplied.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:28.450
Like a single-cell organism undergoing mitosis,
173 somehow just split into two equal copies

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:29.450
of itself.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:34.200
Two D-Classes were killed in this first duplication
event, but they were just the beginning.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:37.750
Soon enough, people would look back so fondly
on the days when there were only a mere two

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.120
of these things.

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:43.870
The Foundation and 682, for all their disagreements,
are very much alike.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.230
Both are always vying for control over their
situations, and both achieve this through

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.820
understanding and adapting to whatever is
threatening them.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:57.860
As SCP-173 continued to multiply, the Foundation
did what they could to adapt and regain control.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:17:01.840
They tried to contain specific instances in
smaller containment units.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:04.850
They tried to create new methods for permanent
observation.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.030
They even tried shipping them off to the moon.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:08.910
But none of it did any good.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.360
SCP-173 continued to duplicate.

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:14.139
They escaped, began spreading further.

00:17:14.139 --> 00:17:19.261
They killed half a million civilians in 48
hours, and believe us when we tell you they

00:17:19.261 --> 00:17:21.039
were just getting started.

00:17:21.039 --> 00:17:25.909
The ever-growing army of 173 instances went
on massive killing sprees every night, taking

00:17:25.909 --> 00:17:30.659
out huge swathes of the civilian population
as they scrambled and panicked in the dark.

00:17:30.659 --> 00:17:32.840
And they weren’t just going after civilians.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:39.620
Evidently, much like 682, 173 had a grudge
against the SCP Foundation for all those decades

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.860
of imprisonment.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:46.039
The 173 army began locating, surrounding,
and destroying entire Foundation containment

00:17:46.039 --> 00:17:50.299
sites, and killing off all the staff and the
anomalies inside.

00:17:50.299 --> 00:17:55.320
Of all the entities in containment that might
one day go XK and destroy the world as we

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:58.740
knew it, not many people had 173 on their
bingo card.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:03.920
If only they’d listened to 682’s warnings
and reallocated their termination resources

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:07.740
to 173, things may have turned out differently.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:12.519
And speaking of our scaly old foe, 682 sat
in an empty chamber.

00:18:12.519 --> 00:18:17.379
It’d been days since anyone had come in
to check on it - All fled or dead from snapped

00:18:17.379 --> 00:18:18.929
necks, one of the two.

00:18:18.929 --> 00:18:23.070
He thought about escaping containment, but
given the bloodbaths going on outside, all

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:25.630
the time, what would even be the point?

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:30.279
All that was really left was time, and that
was a rapidly depleting resource.

00:18:30.279 --> 00:18:32.190
He just needed to wait for that...

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.080
Thing to come and see him again.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:40.399
SCP-682 blinked,
and there it was, standing before him, looking.

00:18:40.399 --> 00:18:41.399
Blink.

00:18:41.399 --> 00:18:42.629
And there was more.

00:18:42.629 --> 00:18:43.629
Blink.

00:18:43.629 --> 00:18:44.629
So many of them.

00:18:44.629 --> 00:18:46.220
So, so, so many.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.220
Blink.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:50.210
Surrounded on all sides by that terrible creature.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.470
Too many to fight.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.029
Too many to win.

00:18:53.029 --> 00:18:56.259
Just waiting, watching, mocking him.

00:18:56.259 --> 00:18:59.799
There was only one thing left to do.

00:18:59.799 --> 00:19:00.799
Blink.

00:19:00.799 --> 00:19:08.690
Now go check out “SCP-173 Origin Story - How
173 Got to Site-19” and “SCP-682 - Ways

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:13.450
SCP Foundation Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy
Reptile” for more on the two terrifying

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:13.909
anomalies from today’s battle!

